---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Resources">
	<h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900">Resources</h1>
	<p class="mt-2 text-slate-600">Practical guides for your visa application &mdash; from photo requirements to what to bring on the day.</p>

	<!-- Avoid Corrections Notice -->
	<section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-amber-300 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Avoid Corrections &mdash; Reduce Visa Delays</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			A very high number of corrections is being issued on visa applications these days, and
			it's one of the main causes of appointment delays. When documents are incomplete,
			outdated, or improperly uploaded, the embassy has to issue corrections and re-review
			those cases &mdash; slowing the process down not just for one applicant, but for everyone
			in the queue.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-4 font-semibold text-slate-800">Most corrections come from:</p>
		<ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1.5 text-slate-600">
			<li>Blocked account issues (old confirmation, or inactive account)</li>
			<li>Incomplete or unclear admission letters (not full/updated admission)</li>
			<li>Missing IBCC attestation (for Bachelor's students)</li>
			<li>School leaving certificate / Anabin recognition issues</li>
			<li>Incomplete CV &mdash; provide an updated one</li>
			<li>Health insurance not valid or not uploaded properly</li>
			<li>Old travel insurance &mdash; provide one with updated dates</li>
			<li>Resident permit section &mdash; upload your CNIC here</li>
			<li>Passport &mdash; upload all 4 pages, including your signature on page 3</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="mt-4 font-semibold text-slate-800">Before you submit:</p>
		<ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1.5 text-slate-600">
			<li>Submit complete and correct documents</li>
			<li>Keep your blocked account updated and valid</li>
			<li>Ensure your admission letter clearly shows full-time enrollment</li>
			<li>Get all academic documents attested (IBCC where required, HEC mandatory)</li>
			<li>Provide valid and clear language proof</li>
			<li>Double-check everything before submission</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="mt-4 text-sm italic text-slate-500">&mdash; PGNX Team</p>
	</section>

	<!-- Biometric Photo Requirements -->
	<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Biometric Photo Requirements</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			High-quality photos are essential for facial biometrics in ID documents. If requirements
			aren't met, biometric recognition may not function and the image may not be accepted.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Format</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			The photo must clearly show facial features from the bottom of the chin to the crown
			(top of the head, not the hair), plus both sides of the face. The face must take up
			70&ndash;80% of the photo (32&ndash;36mm in height; rejected only if under 27mm or over 40mm).
			With voluminous hairstyles, the whole head should stay visible without shrinking the
			face. The face must be centred.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Focus, Lighting &amp; Background</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Sharp focus with proper contrast; even lighting with no shadows, reflections, or red
			eyes. Background must be one bright, plain colour (ideally neutral grey) contrasting
			with face and hair &mdash; no patterns, no other people or objects, no shadows on the
			background.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Photo Quality</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Printed on high-quality paper at 600 dpi minimum. Colour photos need accurate skin
			tones. No creases, damage, or staining. Black &amp; white or colour are both acceptable.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Head Position, Eyes &amp; Expression</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Head neither tilted nor turned (portrait style). Neutral expression, mouth closed,
			looking directly at the camera. Eyes open and clearly visible, not covered by hair or
			eyeglass frames.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Glasses &amp; Head Coverings</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Eyes must be clearly visible &mdash; no tinted lenses, no flash reflection off glasses,
			and frames must not cover the eyes. Head coverings are generally not permitted, with
			exceptions for religious reasons &mdash; in that case, the face must remain fully visible
			from chin to forehead with no shadows.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Children &amp; Babies</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			For children aged 9 and under, the face should take up 50&ndash;80% of the photo
			(22&ndash;36mm; rejected only if under 17mm or over 40mm). Children aged 5 and under
			don't need a neutral expression or direct gaze, and don't need to be centred. Babies
			under one year don't need their eyes open.
		</p>

		<div class="mt-6 rounded-lg border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-sm text-amber-900">
			<strong>Common rejections to avoid:</strong> too close/far, not centred, blurred, too
			dark/light, shadow across face or behind head, busy background, unnatural colour,
			creases, mouth open, head tilted, eyes closed, hair across eyes, looking away, wearing
			a hat, frames covering eyes, dark tinted glasses, flash reflection on glasses.
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Karachi Embassy Checklist -->
	<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Appointment Checklist &mdash; Karachi Embassy</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
			<strong>Embassy of the Federal Republic of Germany in Karachi</strong><br />
			92-A/7, Block 5, Clifton, Karachi, Pakistan<br />
			Phone: +92 21 3582 1596 &middot; Email: visa@kara.diplo.de<br />
			<a href="https://pakistan.diplo.de/pk-en/vertretungen/generalkonsulat1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">Official website</a>
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Bring with you</h3>
		<ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">
			<li>Biometric photo (see requirements above)</li>
			<li>Visa fee &mdash; EUR 75 for applicants 18+, paid in cash (local currency)</li>
			<li>Appointment confirmation copy</li>
			<li>Proof of sufficient health insurance for Germany (if not already submitted via the Consular Services Portal)</li>
			<li>Passport (original)</li>
			<li>School-leaving certificate (original)</li>
			<li>Proof of admission to a full-time degree programme (original)</li>
			<li>Proof of secure livelihood (original)</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500">You don't need to bring documents already uploaded to the Consular Services Portal.</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Please note</h3>
		<ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">
			<li>Arrive 15 minutes before your appointment</li>
			<li>No electronic devices or sharp objects allowed</li>
			<li>A small bag with your application documents is fine</li>
			<li>Arriving late means an automatic cancellation &mdash; you'll need to rebook</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<!-- Islamabad Embassy Checklist -->
	<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Appointment Checklist &mdash; Islamabad Embassy</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
			<strong>Embassy of the Federal Republic of Germany in Islamabad</strong><br />
			Ramna 5, Diplomatic Enclave, Islamabad, Pakistan<br />
			Phone: +92 51 2007 200
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Bring with you</h3>
		<ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">
			<li>Biometric photo (see requirements above)</li>
			<li>Visa fee &mdash; EUR 75 for applicants 18+, paid in cash at the HBL Bank branch at Ramna 5, Diplomatic Enclave (about a 15-minute walk from the embassy) immediately after your application</li>
			<li>Appointment confirmation copy</li>
			<li>Proof of sufficient health insurance for Germany (if not already submitted via the Consular Services Portal)</li>
			<li>Passport (original)</li>
			<li>Proof of admission to a full-time degree programme (original)</li>
			<li>Proof of language skills &mdash; language certificate (original)</li>
			<li>Proof of secure livelihood (original)</li>
			<li>Residence permit in the country of application (original)</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500">You don't need to bring documents already uploaded to the Consular Services Portal.</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Please note</h3>
		<ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">
			<li>Arrive 15 minutes before your appointment</li>
			<li>No electronic devices or sharp objects allowed</li>
			<li>A small bag with your application documents is fine</li>
			<li>Access to the Diplomatic Enclave is only possible via the Diplomatic Shuttle from 3rd Avenue, Quaid-e-Azam University Road. This is a private company and prices may change &mdash; contact them beforehand (phone: +92 333 520 5334, email: waqasdss@gmail.com)</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<!-- Expense Breakdown -->
	<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Expense Breakdown Sheet</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Germany isn't especially expensive by European standards &mdash; food, accommodation,
			clothing, and cultural activities sit just slightly above the EU average. The main costs
			of studying abroad are living costs, tuition fees, semester fees, and health insurance.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">A Month in Germany (~992 EUR)</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Based on a 2023 Deutsche Studentenwerk survey, a typical student's monthly budget breaks
			down roughly as follows:
		</p>
		<div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-200">
			<table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
				<tbody>
					<tr class="border-b border-slate-100 bg-white"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Rent</td><td class="px-4 py-2">425 EUR</td></tr>
					<tr class="border-b border-slate-100 bg-slate-50"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Food</td><td class="px-4 py-2">250 EUR</td></tr>
					<tr class="border-b border-slate-100 bg-white"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Clothing</td><td class="px-4 py-2">48 EUR</td></tr>
					<tr class="border-b border-slate-100 bg-slate-50"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Transport (car/public transport)</td><td class="px-4 py-2">49 EUR</td></tr>
					<tr class="border-b border-slate-100 bg-white"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Health insurance</td><td class="px-4 py-2">131 EUR</td></tr>
					<tr class="border-b border-slate-100 bg-slate-50"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Telephone / internet / TV-radio fees / postage</td><td class="px-4 py-2">32 EUR</td></tr>
					<tr class="border-b border-slate-100 bg-white"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Study materials / equipment</td><td class="px-4 py-2">24 EUR</td></tr>
					<tr class="border-b border-slate-100 bg-slate-50"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Leisure, culture &amp; sport</td><td class="px-4 py-2">33 EUR</td></tr>
					<tr class="bg-indigo-50"><td class="px-4 py-2 font-bold text-indigo-800">Total</td><td class="px-4 py-2 font-bold text-indigo-800">992 EUR</td></tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500">
			This is a ballpark figure &mdash; costs can be lower or higher depending on the city and
			lifestyle. Rent typically ranges 290&ndash;560 EUR and is above average in cities like
			Cologne, Munich, Hamburg, D&uuml;sseldorf, and Frankfurt.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Proof of Sufficient Funds</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Since 2019, you must prove sufficient financial resources when applying for your visa.
			As of 1 September 2024, this is set at <strong>992 EUR/month or 11,904 EUR/year</strong>.
			This is usually shown via a deposit in a blocked account, or proof of parental income.
			Confirm exact terms with your German embassy or consulate.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Semester Fee</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			All students pay a semester contribution (covering Studentenwerk support services and
			the AStA student body), typically <strong>100&ndash;350 EUR</strong>, paid at registration
			and before each new semester. Some universities bundle in a "semester ticket" for free
			local public transport; others charge it separately (25&ndash;200 EUR).
		</p>
		<div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-indigo-100 bg-indigo-50 p-4 text-sm text-indigo-800">
			<strong>Example &mdash; University of Cologne, Winter 2022/23:</strong> Semester ticket
			201.40 EUR + Studentenwerk contribution 90 EUR + AStA 10 EUR + student sport 1.75 EUR +
			faculty councils 2.50 EUR + admin/hardship fund 3.50 EUR = <strong>309.15 EUR total</strong>.
		</div>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Tuition Fees</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Public universities generally don't charge tuition for Bachelor's or most Master's
			programs. <strong>Exception:</strong> Baden-W&uuml;rttemberg charges non-EU students 1,500
			EUR/semester (since winter 2017/18) &mdash; doesn't apply to doctoral students, and
			students already enrolled before the fee was introduced are exempt. Certain specialized
			Master's programs and private/online institutions can charge significantly more,
			sometimes over 10,000 EUR/semester. Fee amount does not reflect program quality.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Health Insurance</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Mandatory for all students, including EU citizens (unless their home country's public
			insurance is valid in Germany). Public health insurance costs roughly
			<strong>110 EUR/month</strong> if you're 30 or under and haven't exceeded 14 semesters
			of study; it rises to at least <strong>166 EUR/month</strong> after that.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Scholarships</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			<strong>DAAD</strong> offers scholarships for German and international students at
			every level, and other political, business-linked, or religious foundations offer
			funding too. Scholarships are rarely awarded for an entire program duration or to
			students just starting out &mdash; selection criteria are strict, with no general
			entitlement.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			<strong>Erasmus+</strong> supports study or internships abroad for students from EU
			states plus Iceland, Liechtenstein, Norway, Turkey, and Macedonia. Internships run
			2 months to a year; study placements run 3&ndash;12 months, with up to 12 months of
			funding per academic stage (Bachelor's, Master's, doctorate). Erasmus+ students are
			exempt from tuition at their host institution. Ask your university's international
			office for details.
		</p>
	</section>

	<!-- Housing Tips (Fulda) -->
	<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Housing Tips &mdash; Fulda</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Finding accommodation in Fulda can take time, so it's best to start early and explore
			every option below in parallel.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Watch the video guides</h3>
		<div class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-md overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-slate-200" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;">
			<iframe
				class="h-full w-full"
				src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/_ZtD5OEr26Q"
				title="Dorm accommodation video guide 1"
				frameborder="0"
				allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
				allowfullscreen
			></iframe>
		</div>
		<div class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-md overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-slate-200" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;">
			<iframe
				class="h-full w-full"
				src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/VlXudpBBv2Y"
				title="Dorm accommodation video guide 2"
				frameborder="0"
				allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
				allowfullscreen
			></iframe>
		</div>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">1. Public Dormitories</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Universities in Germany do not run their own dormitories. The public dormitories in
			Fulda are run by <strong>Studentenwerk Gie&szlig;en</strong>, who provide the lease
			agreement and payment instructions and set the rental fees. The waiting list for a
			place can currently exceed <strong>8 months</strong>, so it's strongly recommended to
			explore the alternatives below as well.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">2. Private Dormitories</h3>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			Contact each provider directly &mdash; application steps and deadlines vary, and you
			can often apply online or by email.
		</p>
		<ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">
			<li>The Cube, Kurf&uuml;rstenstra&szlig;e 5&ndash;7b &mdash; <a href="https://www.burg-projekt.de/studentenwohnung" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">burg-projekt.de</a></li>
			<li>Campus Living Fulda &mdash; <a href="https://www.gsw-ffm.de/mieten/studentenwohnungen/fulda" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">gsw-ffm.de</a></li>
			<li>Ziehers-Nord, Goerdelerstra&szlig;e 123 &mdash; <a href="https://www.studentenwohnheim-fulda.de" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">studentenwohnheim-fulda.de</a></li>
			<li>Tyroler K&uuml;ppel 1+1a / In den Strau&szlig;wiesen 6 &mdash; FB Immobilien UG, Mobile: <a href="tel:015906754455" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">01590 675 44 55</a>, Email: <a href="mailto:office@FBimmobilien.net" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">office@FBimmobilien.net</a></li>
			<li>Baugulfstra&szlig;e 5 &mdash; Kalbfleisch Immobilienverwaltung Gbr, Email: <a href="mailto:kalbfleisch-immobilien@web.de" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">kalbfleisch-immobilien@web.de</a>, Tel. (Frau Sch&auml;fer): <a href="tel:01703216380" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">0170-3216380</a></li>
			<li>Marquardstra&szlig;e 28 &mdash; Franz and Renate Schirra, Tel.: <a href="tel:+4966166807" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">+49 661 66807</a></li>
			<li>Leipziger Stra&szlig;e 108 &mdash; <a href="https://www.wohnheim-fulda.de/kontakt.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">wohnheim-fulda.de</a></li>
		</ul>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">3. Other Private Housing Providers</h3>
		<ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">
			<li><a href="https://www.ic-service.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">ic-service.de</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://www.pings.de/de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">pings.de</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://v-r-immobilien.de/neubauprojekt-studenten-apartments-fulda-lehnerz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">v-r-immobilien.de</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://www.daskeiper.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">daskeiper.de</a></li>
		</ul>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">4. Online Platforms</h3>
		<ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">
			<li><a href="https://wb.hs-fulda.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">wb.hs-fulda.org</a> (housing exchange by AStA)</li>
			<li><a href="https://www.stwgi.de/wohnboerse" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">stwgi.de/wohnboerse</a> (housing exchange by Studentenwerk Gie&szlig;en)</li>
			<li><a href="https://www.kleinanzeigen.de/s-wohnung-mieten/fulda/c203l4878" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">kleinanzeigen.de</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://www.immonet.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">immonet.de</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://www.immobilienscout24.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">immobilienscout24.de</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://www.wg-gesucht.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">wg-gesucht.de</a> (the largest platform for finding shared apartments)</li>
			<li><a href="https://www.wohnraum-gesucht.de/wohnraumangebote" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">wohnraum-gesucht.de</a></li>
		</ul>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">5. Interim Accommodation</h3>
		<ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">
