	<!-- Steps to Visit the German Embassy -->
	<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Steps to Visit the German Embassy (Islamabad)</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			A walk-through of what actually happens on your appointment day, from parking to
			leaving the embassy.
		</p>

		<ol class="mt-4 list-inside list-decimal space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			<li><strong>Mobile phone &amp; bag:</strong> after parking, go to a waiting room about 2 minutes away, submit your bag and mobile, and get a token. If someone is with you, hand it to them.</li>
			<li><strong>Enter the shuttle service:</strong> security guards will check your appointment email letter and let you in.</li>
			<li><strong>Waiting hall (again):</strong> wait 5&ndash;10 minutes. Shuttle service tickets start being distributed here.</li>
			<li><strong>Token line:</strong> get a token by showing your ID card copy and appointment email copy.</li>
			<li><strong>QR code shuttle ticket:</strong> show your token, pay Rs. 1500, and get a ticket.</li>
			<li><strong>Waiting area (again):</strong> wait in another area; you'll be called after about 2 minutes.</li>
			<li><strong>German Embassy arrival:</strong> board the bus, arriving after 10&ndash;15 minutes; walk about 2 minutes to the embassy gate.</li>
			<li><strong>Embassy:</strong> your name and appointment details are checked against a list. Sit near the front to be called sooner.</li>
			<li><strong>Attendance:</strong> at the next counter, your passport and appointment are checked again.</li>
			<li><strong>Next line:</strong> you'll be sent to another line and called "next."</li>
			<li><strong>Security check:</strong> remove your belt, wallet, and documents and pass through a scanner; items are returned afterward.</li>
			<li><strong>Embassy counters room:</strong> at a table before the 4 counters, pay Rs. 500 for a courier service, give your address and 2 phone numbers, and get a receipt plus your passport back, along with a token (201, 202, 203, etc.).</li>
			<li><strong>Wait for your call:</strong> when your token is called at counter 1 or 2, you'll have your interview with a visa officer, who takes your fee and passport.</li>
			<li><strong>Back to the shuttle terminal:</strong> after the interview, exit and wait for the bus back to where you started; your ticket is collected as you exit.</li>
		</ol>

		<p class="mt-4 text-sm italic text-slate-500">
			Note: this account was compiled from the experiences of several community members and
			may vary slightly by appointment day.
		</p>
	</section>

