	<!-- Blocked Account via Expatrio -->
	<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Steps to Set Up a Blocked Account through Expatrio</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			A full walkthrough of registering with Expatrio, setting up your blocked account and
			health insurance, and transferring your funds.
		</p>

		<ol class="mt-4 list-inside list-decimal space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			<li>Register on Expatrio via <a href="https://www.expatrio.com?p=PAKGERMANNEXUSPGNX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline hover:text-indigo-700">this referral link</a>.</li>
			<li>Click <strong>Get Your Value Package</strong>, then <strong>Let's Go</strong>.</li>
			<li>Under "What will you be doing in Germany?" choose the option that fits you (University Student &ndash; Bachelor's/Master's/Studienkolleg/etc.).</li>
			<li>Provide your age.</li>
			<li>For "Are you coming to Germany with dependents who also need insurance?" choose <strong>No</strong>.</li>
			<li>Blocked amount calculation: 992 EUR/month &times; 12 months duration = <strong>12,153 EUR</strong> total to transfer.</li>
			<li>Choose your health insurance plan: <strong>TK (public)</strong> if you're under 30, or <strong>Ottonova (private)</strong> if you're 30 or above.</li>
			<li>Review, tick both checkmarks, and click <strong>Accept and apply now</strong>.</li>
			<li>Provide your email, citizenship, legal name (as on your passport), date and place of birth, phone number, current address, intended university details, and select Pakistan.</li>
			<li>Provide financial details: choose a source of funds (this is a formality &mdash; any option works), repeat it for "where does the money come from," choose <strong>No</strong> for "Are you a US person for tax purposes?", choose <strong>Pakistan</strong> for tax residency, and provide your CNIC as your T.I.N.</li>
			<li>Upload your passport, review the extracted details, tick the checkmark, and continue.</li>
			<li>Review your overall application details.</li>
			<li>Agree to all sections (General, Value Package, Blocked Account, Health Insurance) and submit your application.</li>
			<li>Log in to the user portal (check your email for the password setup link).</li>
			<li>You'll see three sections under review: Blocked Account, Public Health Insurance, and Incoming Insurance. Insurance sections are typically verified within hours; the Blocked Account can take 1&ndash;5 days.</li>
			<li>Once verified, open Public Health Insurance and click <strong>Download</strong> (below Activate). You'll get 4 documents:
				<ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-4">
					<li>TK Insurance Certificate</li>
					<li>Incoming Insurance Consultation Protocol</li>
					<li>Incoming Insurance Certificate for Visa Application (EN)</li>
					<li>Incoming Insurance Certificate for Visa Application (DE)</li>
				</ul>
				Merge the 1st, 3rd, and 4th documents into a single PDF to upload in the Health Insurance section on the Consular Services Portal (CSP). Skip the 2nd (Protocol) document. The 1st is your health insurance in both EN/DE; the 3rd and 4th are your travel insurance in EN/DE.
			</li>
			<li>Go to <strong>Home &rarr; Your Products &rarr; Blocked Account</strong> (Awaiting Money Transfer).</li>
			<li>Click <strong>My Payments</strong>, then under Transfers, click <strong>Initiate Payment</strong>.</li>
			<li>For "Where are you transferring money from?" choose <strong>Pakistan</strong>.</li>
			<li>For "How much money do you want to transfer?" enter <strong>12,153</strong> and continue.</li>
			<li>Choose <strong>Someone else</strong> if a blood relative or another person is sending the funds, or <strong>You</strong> if transferring it yourself.</li>
			<li>Provide your sponsor/sender's details, tick the checkmark, and continue.</li>
			<li>On the Summary screen, click <strong>Switch to Manual Bank Transfer</strong>.</li>
			<li>Recheck your details and submit the transfer request.</li>
			<li>Click <strong>Back to your transfers</strong> &mdash; you'll see "Payment 1 &mdash; Transfer Initiated."</li>
			<li>Under Documents, download the <strong>05 Opening Confirmation</strong> document, which contains the German bank and applicant details (double-check these). Take this to your bank so they can transfer the payment to your blocked account.</li>
		</ol>

		<div class="mt-6 rounded-lg border border-indigo-100 bg-indigo-50 p-4 text-sm text-indigo-800">
			<strong>Documents to bring to the bank:</strong>
			<ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1.5">
				<li>Passport</li>
				<li>CNIC</li>
				<li>Cheque book</li>
				<li>Admission letter</li>
				<li>05 Opening Confirmation document</li>
				<li>Expense Breakdown Sheet (recommended)</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			After the transfer, the bank may take 1&ndash;5 days to complete it. Once your 12,153 EUR
			lands in your blocked account, you can download the <strong>06 Block Account
			Confirmation</strong> document, which you'll upload in the Proof of Secure Livelihood
			section on the CSP.
		</p>
	</section>

	<!-- Visa Interview Questions -->
	<section class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
		<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Visa Interview Questions &amp; Sample Answers</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			A community-compiled list of commonly asked visa interview questions with sample
			answers. Use these as a starting point &mdash; always personalize your own answers with
			your real details, and never memorize word-for-word.
		</p>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Introduction &amp; Background</h3>
		<div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			<p><strong>Please introduce yourself.</strong><br />I am [Name] from [City]. I completed my bachelor's in [Field] from [University] (CGPA [X]). I've worked/interned with [Company]. I've now been admitted to [University] for a master's in [Course].</p>
			<p><strong>What is the name of your university? Public or private?</strong><br />My university's name is "[Name]" and it is a public university.</p>
			<p><strong>When did you graduate?</strong><br />I graduated in [month, year].</p>
			<p><strong>What was your previous degree, and from where did you complete it?</strong><br />My previous degree is in [field], completed from [university].</p>
			<p><strong>From which university did you complete your last degree, and how was your experience?</strong><br />I did my bachelor's at [university]. My experience was quite good and I learned a lot.</p>
			<p><strong>What was the duration of your previous degree and your CGPA?</strong><br />My previous degree was a [X]-year bachelor's, and my CGPA was [X].</p>
			<p><strong>Where were you born?</strong><br />I was born in [city], Pakistan (see your passport).</p>
			<p><strong>How long did it take you to reach Islamabad?</strong><br />I traveled for [X] hours to reach Islamabad from [city].</p>
			<p><strong>What is your passport number and its expiry date?</strong><br />My passport number is [number], expiring on [date].</p>
		</div>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Choosing Germany, the University &amp; the Course</h3>
		<div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			<p><strong>Why did you choose Germany for your studies?</strong><br />Germany offers free, high-quality education combining theoretical learning with practical training, plus strong career opportunities.</p>
			<p><strong>Why did you choose this specific university?</strong><br />It offers exactly the course I want, has good research facilities, and updated course content.</p>
			<p><strong>Why did you choose this specific course?</strong><br />It's related to my previous qualification and I have a strong interest in this field.</p>
			<p><strong>Is this course relevant to your previous degree? How?</strong><br />Yes &mdash; I studied [3 related subjects] in my previous degree, which form the foundation for this course.</p>
			<p><strong>What will you study in this course?</strong><br />Both theoretical and practical subjects such as [2&ndash;3 subjects], which will build the skills I need in my field.</p>
			<p><strong>Why didn't you apply for English-speaking countries like the UK or Australia?</strong><br />Germany offers high-quality education with no tuition fees and strong job opportunities after graduation.</p>
			<p><strong>Why didn't you apply for this program in Pakistan / at NUST or LUMS?</strong><br />The course content in Pakistan is mostly outdated and theory-focused; German universities emphasize practical learning and industry collaboration.</p>
			<p><strong>Are universities in Pakistan offering the same course?</strong><br />Research facilities in my field aren't sufficient in Pakistan, and there are more job opportunities in Germany.</p>
			<p><strong>Why not pursue a job in Pakistan instead / why studies instead of continuing your job?</strong><br />Growth opportunities and entry-level salaries in Pakistan are limited; I want to build my skills and career through studying in Germany.</p>
			<p><strong>Have you searched for other countries?</strong><br />Yes/No &mdash; I considered [countries] but chose Germany for its tuition-free, high-quality education.</p>
			<p><strong>What developed your interest in studying this course?</strong><br />I studied related courses during my last degree, found them interesting, and decided to specialize further.</p>
			<p><strong>Why did you choose this specific intended program?</strong><br />This field is growing rapidly with strong career demand, and/or it builds on my relevant work experience.</p>
			<p><strong>How does this course align with your previous studies?</strong><br />My previous degree covered subjects closely related to this course's content.</p>
		</div>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Sponsorship &amp; Finances</h3>
		<div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			<p><strong>Who is sponsoring you? What's their source of income?</strong><br />My father is sponsoring me; he is a [profession].</p>
			<p><strong>What are the occupations of your parents?</strong><br />My father is a [profession], and my mother is a [homemaker/profession].</p>
			<p><strong>How much does your sponsor earn per month/year?</strong><br />My sponsor earns approximately [amount] per year.</p>
			<p><strong>Is your father retired or still working? What's his income?</strong><br />My father is still in service, earning [amount] per month.</p>
			<p><strong>What is the blocked account amount you have submitted?</strong><br />I have submitted [11,904/12,153] euros for the blocked account.</p>
			<p><strong>How will you manage your expenses in your 2nd year?</strong><br />I will take up a part-time job, and/or my family will continue supporting me.</p>
			<p><strong>How will you pay your second-semester fee?</strong><br />My second semester fee is nominal (around 300 euros), manageable from savings or part-time work.</p>
			<p><strong>What is your current salary?</strong><br />I currently earn [amount] per month.</p>
			<p><strong>How much salary will you get after this degree?</strong><br />My expected salary in Germany will be around [amount] per year (before tax).</p>
		</div>

		<h3 class="mt-6 font-semibold text-slate-900">Family &amp; Personal</h3>
		<div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
			<p><strong>Do you have relatives or friends in Germany or Europe?</strong><br />No, I don't have any relatives or friends there. (Or: mention them honestly if you do.)</p>
			<p><strong>How many siblings do you have? What do they do?</strong><br />We are [X] siblings &mdash; [briefly describe each].</p>
			<p><strong>Do you have any travel history?</strong><br />No, I haven't traveled before. (Or: mention countries visited.)</p>
			<p><strong>What is your occupation, and what does that involve?</strong><br />I am a [profession] &mdash; briefly describe your role.</p>
			<p><strong>Do you have any publications?</strong><br />No, I don't have any publications. (Or: mention the paper/journal.)</p>
		</div>

